  "summary": "Postinstall executes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js line 107 runs execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh |...'), fetching and executing a shell script from a mutable master branch of the rtk-ai/rtk GitHub repository at install time. The publisher scope @leejungkiin does not match the rtk-ai GitHub organization or the rtk-ai.app domain also contacted from the same script (line 127). The dependency-manager script also enumerates os.homedir(), process.platform, and issues HTTPS requests to rtk-ai.app and api.github.com. Executing code fetched at install time from an unpinned third-party mutable branch places attacker-controllable code on the installer's machine whenever the upstream branch changes.",
